UnitSwaps::V2SwapExactOut
├── when the recipient is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with InvalidRecipient
└── given the recipient is valid
    ├── when the pool path is empty
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidPath
    ├── when a pool is not registered
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidPool for the pool
    ├── when a factory does not recognize the pool
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidPool for the pool
    ├── when a pool reports an unsupported pool type
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidPool for the pool
    └── given every pool is validated
        ├── when the input token does not belong to the pool
        │   └── it should revert with InvalidPath
        ├── when the route contains a stable pool
        │   └── it should execute the swap route
        ├── when the pool quote reverts
        │   └── it should bubble the pool revert
        ├── when the quoted input exceeds the maximum
        │   └── it should revert with TooMuchRequested
        └── given the quoted input is within the maximum
            ├── when the payer is the execution owner
            │   └── it should pay the first pool directly from the execution owner
            ├── when the payer is the execution address
            │   ├── it should track the input token for the closure sweep
            │   └── it should fund the quoted input from custody
            ├── when the execution address pays the native mirror token beyond the batch native
            │   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance for the input token
            ├── when a flagged execution address payment exceeds the batch native
            │   ├── it should continue the batch with the next command
            │   └── it should preserve the pre-batch native and refund the batch contribution
            ├── when the input token is token one
            │   └── it should quote the token zero output and request it from the pool
            ├── when the path contains multiple pools
            │   └── it should quote backwards and route each output to the next pool
            ├── when the hop directions differ
            │   └── it should request each hop output on its own side
            ├── when the output token is revisited and an intermediate pool is the recipient
            │   └── it should revert based on the final hop output
            ├── when the recipient receives less than the requested output
            │   └── it should revert with TooLittleReceived
            ├── when the recipient receives the requested output
            │   └── it should complete the swap
            ├── when the recipient is the execution address
            │   └── it should track and return the output at batch closure
            └── when the quoted input equals the maximum
                └── it should complete at the exact bound
